prompt: >
  Continue in E:\Source\Rust\SLMComposer.com as the active Rust workspace for TinyRustLM, with E:\Source\Rust\MiniModel.org as the MiniModel.org site workspace. The site-folder split, source-control cleanup, MiniModel intake processing, Hugging Face option routing, roadmap, metadata-only MiniModel catalog endpoint, TinyRustLM catalog-to-local-file import slice, Chat/Advanced Tools dashboard redesign, local Hugging Face conversion-script handoff, Rust `.minimodel-peer-offer` proof commands, the first MiniModel local Rust verifier (`minimodel-core` plus `minimodel` CLI), local peer-piece export/reassembly, TinyRustLM.com root app route, and Hugging Face/P2P enterprise quality refactor are complete in local source. TinyRustLM.com and documentation sites should be deployed from source only after docs are updated and live proof is run. Start the next work by deciding the smallest consent-based network prototype that can move existing peer pieces between consenting peers and then call `assemble-peer-pieces` plus `verify-artifact` without adding project-server model bytes. Keep TinyRustLM browser-local and keep project servers metadata-only: no server-side user model execution and no project-server user model bytes.
primary_goal: >
  Move from local peer-piece export/reassembly into the first consent-based peer-transfer network design slice while preserving the verifier as the authority: peers may provide chunks later, but local Rust verification and receipts remain mandatory before TinyRustLM import.
