roadmap_guardrails:
  - Rust-first P2P model exchange architecture; evaluate Pear/Bare/Hyper as tradeoffs, not core SLMComposer dependencies.
  - Source options are user-owned local files/lists, user-triggered Hugging Face discovery, and future MiniModel P2P transfer; all converge on local `.slm` verification.
  - SLMComposer Chat mode should keep Local Files, Hugging Face, P2P Exchange, prompt, and Generate visible on first load while Advanced Tools exposes diagnostics and lower-level controls.
  - SLMComposer dashboard source should remain simple on first load: left navigation, local privacy proof, model-ready toolbar, starter cards, central composer, and contained Advanced Options for pro controls.
  - Hugging Face rows are model-card metadata only; simple rows use a list-level P2P toggle, show `P2P Import` only for peer-proof MiniModel matches while P2P is enabled, show `Start Conversion` otherwise, show one disabled-P2P warning, and keep Search Metadata from closing the source chooser.
  - Keep TinyRustLM.com `/` as the canonical public app route; `/app/` can remain a secondary route, but docs and deploy proof should target root.
  - Keep the Hugging Face UI row state centralized through shared helpers; do not reintroduce divergent simple/advanced compatibility text or per-row simple conversion controls.
  - Legal/liability boundaries must keep MiniModel.org as metadata/catalog guidance until legal review; no claims that third-party models are safe, legal, or endorsed.
  - Secure manifests must be checksum-bound and route source identity, model cards, license, tokenizer/config, eval/admission evidence, chunk/Merkle data, and signatures.
  - Tiny-model creation/import stays tied to TinyRustLM local review, conversion, validation, runtime-smoke, eval, admission, and local import receipts.
  - Project servers never run user model bytes and never serve user model bytes.
next_implementation_slice:
  - Preserve the implemented `key=value` manifest parser, duplicate-key rejection, project-server model-byte URL rejection, and server-execution rejection as the non-negotiable trust gate.
  - Design the smallest peer-transfer prototype around existing `.minimodel-peer-offer` chunk proofs, manifest v0 chunk/Merkle fields, `minimodel.peer_piece_set.v0`, `assemble-peer-pieces`, and `minimodel verify-artifact` revalidation.
  - Mirror the TinyRustLM catalog-import proof: catalog metadata can name expectations, but local verifier artifacts must come from user-supplied local paths or consent-based peer chunks reassembled locally.
  - Preserve the Hugging Face boundary: metadata discovery is allowed, project-server byte proxying and remote inference execution are not.
  - Keep any peer-transfer receipt path on `user-selected-tinyrustlm-local-file-open` after local verification passes.
  - Keep DHTs, relays, and desktop UI optional until the direct manifest/peer-offer/local-reverify path is stable.
success_criteria:
  - Active intake buckets remain empty or placeholder-only.
  - SLMComposer.com remains browser-local and user-selected local `.slm` import remains the model byte boundary.
  - MiniModel.org local schema parsing, verifier checks, peer-piece export/reassembly, and receipt writing remain stable; metadata-only catalog is current and live peer networking remains the next later phase.
  - MiniModel local verifier tests and CLI smokes remain green before any peer-transfer behavior is trusted.
  - Long-term memory remains pointer-based and checksum-bearing.
  - Before claiming completion, run relevant pointer audits and `git diff --check`.
